5.text:
The net on g5 is already complete.

* g6 is occupied by the …g6+ pawn and f5/h5 are hit by the g-pawn;
* g4 is hit by the e5 knight;
* h4/h6 are hit by the h2 rook;
* f4 is occupied by the White Nf4;
* Kxh5 is illegal on g6-pawn/rook cover.

1…Rh2-h5+ is therefore check on the g-file.
Kxh5 is illegal on …g6, Kh6/Kh4 are on the rook line, Kg4 is hit by Ne5, Kf5 is hit by …g6 and Kf4 is occupied by Nf4. The only nominal flight f6 is covered in the actual board, so the rook check is mate on the move.

Rh5#

